{"title":"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a49696e74b8b660b8c2f4cbcfde366378b5141a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{2,7,15,26,\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> be the set of all numbers for which the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> element in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> triangular number and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> positive perfect square. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the set which contains all unique remainders when the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Find the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20a781be9018f13b6f38454ef2c1b5abe0f9154a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022=2\\cdot3\\cdot337$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e7218f23fcc3ca422dac71ac6414a2241adfff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_i=\\frac{i(i+1)}{2}+i^2=\\frac{3i^2+i}{2}.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"39\" /> We analyze the possible residues of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> modulo each prime factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. From direct checking, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> attains all residues modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4bb13f188c6b23f37880c1c3cebfdcc415c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$337$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is prime, we work modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4bb13f188c6b23f37880c1c3cebfdcc415c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$337$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33c5cd87f687ae41380698c971a524f270d4887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3i^2+i\\pmod{337}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. Suppose there exist distinct residues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088b2a4cac966f500e82e004b5b9a761a3bd5a37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3a^2+a}{2}\\equiv\\frac{3b^2+b}{2}\\pmod{337},\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"39\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e929380e9c78a5aaa5b93b631970a7fe3e406d49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(3a^2+a)-(3b^2+b)}{2}\\equiv0\\pmod{337}.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"39\" /> Simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec912a47820a4bdf9ba01d3ace80b6227f0b70b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(3a+3b+1)(a-b)\\equiv0\\pmod{337},\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"18\" /> so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18c60d7d33b7407a1b630a8f55755407bb16ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ne b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b7049b37af84c9aabb7f66483911bc0cea4a58fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a+3b+1\\equiv0\\pmod{337}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/79474ae7e767b76f5e19ecf15c3f975ee05df997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\equiv112\\pmod{337}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, for each residue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0350538e594c95fa21a332c3804123e4b6bac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\not\\equiv56\\pmod{337}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, there is a unique distinct residue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> mapping to the same value, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61a3f88c95abd96030196d1ba152460c2a4d9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> maps to itself. Therefore, the number of distinct residues modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4bb13f188c6b23f37880c1c3cebfdcc415c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$337$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43c727f435807721b4d11b867653f980cc92dd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{337+1}{2}=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />, and the total number of distinct residues modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31616ea25b0aa660c23c9b696086974a10c0baf8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cdot3\\cdot169=\\boxed{1014}.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022129\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 128/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6115/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24743:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022129 and revision id 280142. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}